# Lesson 3: Data Cleaning

This lesson focused on handling missing data and correcting data types.

```python
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

# Creating a DataFrame with missing values
data = {
    "Name": ["Tom", "Jerry", np.nan],
    "Score": [85, np.nan, 75]
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# Fill missing values
df_filled = df.fillna({"Name": "Unknown", "Score": df["Score"].mean()})
print(df_filled)
```